  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "RIGGER",
   "text": "If the Noble Lie isn't secret, then why is it called a lie?",
   "wav": "pilot/ep10/v07.wav",
   "d": 3.9,
   "e": "00vxxzzwxyyuwvqvsts3gzwzwvslzutwpd000000"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "STERLING",
   "text": "And what are they asking for?",
   "wav": "pilot/ep10/v08.wav",
   "d": 2.025,
   "e": "0000oyzwg45rztzuyzv3ryyoq6oqn8msvk300000"
  },
  {
   "k": "intro",
   "who": "REGENT CREED"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "REGENT CREED",
   "text": "Representation.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep10/v10.wav",
   "d": 2.075,
   "e": "00000009uzz8bwzotupk6erumegef40000000000"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "STERLING",
   "text": "Say it plainly.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep10/v11.wav",
   "d": 1.375,
   "e": "00000emtzxvvwp2005etzzwyxxwpsoke60000000"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "REGENT CREED",
   "text": "Voting. Seats. Input. \"Democracy.\"",
   "wav": "pilot/ep10/v12.wav",
   "d": 3.65,
   "e": "0000lzxmuqlwqea0zzoql5000qyzqnqml6000000"
  },
  {
   "k": "chorus",
   "ask": "we want a say in who runs things",
   "who": "A CITIZEN",
   "v": "https://pub-075ff01374c04555b51c9bc50f258b42.r2.dev/sources/family-life/clips/0000167734-0000182683.mp4",
   "in": 13.24,
   "d": 1.83,
   "said": "We have money to handle.",
   "src": "Family Life",
   "y": 1949
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "STERLING",
   "text": "Democracy is not rule by the people. It's rule by the loudest hunger. A democracy of appetites.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep10/v14.wav",
   "d": 7.125,
   "e": "0yztssxxqzvxpuh00umyztwwzpwp20vzvtytoth0"
  },
  {
   "k": "narr",
   "text": "His answer is an old story from Plato, the Myth of the Metals. Bronze builds, Silver defends, Gold thinks. Each citizen born to a place.",
   "see": [
    "a billboard beside a highway",
    "workers on a construction site",
    "soldiers marching in formation"
   ],
   "mood": "dread",
   "wav": "pilot/ep10/v15.wav",
   "d": 10.325,
   "e": "0zxxxvwuxtwzytk0vyxwbyyxvozwp0vqzyyvwm00",
   "shots": [
    {
     "v": "https://pub-075ff01374c04555b51c9bc50f258b42.r2.dev/sources/1c5b02f7-87bb-5b3e-9c3d-a6758f606490/v4-conditional-luna-1/clips/08995868-0980-5c02-9fc7-8c5528b4b74a.mp4",
     "in": 0.0,
     "dur": 5.01,
     "src": "Belmont Historical Society Presents: Richard Betts Remembers, PART II ",
     "y": 2006,
     "q": "a billboard beside a highway",
     "fit": 0.278
    },
    {
     "v": "https://pub-075ff01374c04555b51c9bc50f258b42.r2.dev/sources/1fe8a902-7685-5732-a2b5-2591ace091ff/v5-windowed-clip-split-1/clips/8d8f760d-ba83-5470-bfb2-678e5a3a6380.mp4",
     "in": 20.0,
     "dur": 28.25,
     "src": "Builders Of The Broad Highway 2",
     "y": null,
     "q": "workers on a construction site",
     "fit": 0.339
    },
    {
     "v": "https://pub-075ff01374c04555b51c9bc50f258b42.r2.dev/sources/preventing-the-spread-of-disease/clips/0000056356-0000062129.mp4",
     "in": 1.5,
     "dur": 5.77,
     "src": "Preventing the Spread of Disease",
     "y": 1940,
     "q": "soldiers marching in formation",
     "fit": 0.35
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "STERLING",
   "text": "The Myth of the Metals does one thing better than any constitution ever has: It makes inequality feel… natural.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep10/v16.wav",
   "d": 8.225,
   "e": "0yzvxtewwvwxzwwvwkttvuye40xwzwzymym0stl0"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "REGENT HART",
   "text": "So the \"only thing keeping the state from descending\" is… branding?",
   "wav": "pilot/ep10/v17.wav",
   "d": 4.5,
   "e": "00wzyvzz4yxguxwjyktsnxwvqrh90pwsj8000000"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "STERLING",
   "text": "It's not branding. It's a boundary. Between those who can delay gratification— and those who would vote to eat the future.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep10/v18.wav",
   "d": 8.3,
   "e": "0vytzta0ywzo200mzyvswywyquspmzxswxipjrj0"
  },
  {
   "k": "narr",
   "text": "Then the Governor questions his own board, the way the old philosopher questioned Athens.",
   "see": [
    {
     "place": "p2a"
    },
    "men in suits around a table"
   ],
   "mood": "tension and suspense",
   "wav": "pilot/ep10/v19.wav",
   "d": 6.275,
   "e": "0nzwxyyvtzwuzxwsf00zxvwwuxsuqwpxtrrkc000",
   "shots": [
    {
     "v": "https://pub-075ff01374c04555b51c9bc50f258b42.r2.dev/sources/e1214fe3-44a9-5a3c-874f-8a8fb0a9913a/v4-conditional-luna-1/clips/86990282-3a90-5d0c-824b-c549ac846c06.mp4",
     "in": 10.0,
     "src": "Years of Grandeur: Alexander Hamilton U.S. Custom House, New York, NY",
     "y": 2007,
     "q": "p2a"
    },
    {
     "v": "https://pub-075ff01374c04555b51c9bc50f258b42.r2.dev/sources/uitstapje-naar-de-kager-plassen/clips/0000334520-0000339320.mp4",
     "in": 0.5,
     "dur": 4.8,
     "src": "Uitstapje naar de Kager-plassen",
     "y": 1922,
     "q": "men in suits around a table",
     "fit": 0.352
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "STERLING",
   "text": "Let's do this Socratically. Answer me: If the Bronze had full power tomorrow, what would they vote for first?",
   "wav": "pilot/ep10/v20.wav",
   "d": 7.325,
   "e": "0tnxvowpg200wusn40uryvrdxmzsxzpwpzvqpwi0"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "REGENT CREED",
   "text": "They'd… take.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep10/v21.wav",
   "d": 1.85,
   "e": "00000000hpzzzxtqqc8000juvod0910000000000"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "STERLING",
   "text": "Take what?",
   "wav": "pilot/ep10/v22.wav",
   "d": 1.125,
   "e": "0000000jiyzvwxk795lmsxyzzwsla07b80000000"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "REGENT CREED",
   "text": "Gold privileges.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep10/v23.wav",
   "d": 2.125,
   "e": "0000000aqzzzxtoj600nyjqmlegd9c0000000000"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "STERLING",
   "text": "And second?",
   "wav": "pilot/ep10/v24.wav",
   "d": 1.3,
   "e": "000000rzzuvrgfjjiglzzys30gzwroie40000000"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "REGENT HART",
   "text": "They'd dismantle the Auxiliaries.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep10/v25.wav",
   "d": 2.375,
   "e": "0000xyhzngzzxbvqxzvkjvwuqlf85c1000000000"
  },
  {
   "k": "talk",
   "who": "STERLING",
   "text": "Exactly. They would vote until the state becomes a mirror of their wants. That's not freedom. That's a buffet with guns.",
   "wav": "pilot/ep10/v26.wav",
   "d": 8.05,
   "e": "0szmnvywzuwswpxyyzxxzgc0wtvxr80yuvyzvyl0"
  },
  {
   "k": "chorus",
   "ask": "if you give people everything they will just want more",
   "who": "A CITIZEN",
   "v": "https://pub-075ff01374c04555b51c9bc50f258b42.r2.dev/sources/5bc2f88e-f5c0-5bf5-bf1e-85642f2eb2c7/v3-ffmpeg-openclip-1/clips/58b5bc8c-7ea8-5c18-9ebc-dddc44f28f36.mp4",
   "in": 4.92,
   "d": 2.55,
   "said": "What do people want?",
   "src": "Things People Want, The",
   "y": 1948
  },
  {
   "k": "narr",
   "text": "Out in the Shadow Zone, poets are drawing crowds. His remedy is a festival: Metals Week. Everyone re-graded, a loyalty broadcast, and a brisket voucher for the Bronze.",
   "see": [
